  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a Human Resources (HR) management system for an organization. This system will support the management of employee and project-related information, facilitating efficient HR operations.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to create a centralized platform to manage employees' personal and professional data, departmental affiliations, positions, salaries, and project assignments. This system aims to streamline HR processes, improve data accessibility, and enhance project management within the organization.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Stakeholders: HR Managers, Department Heads, Project Managers, IT Administrators.\n- Users: HR Personnel, Employees, Project Managers, Department Supervisors.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Employee Management: Allow HR personnel to record and update employee personal details, department affiliations, and position information. Maintain accurate records of employees' roles and associated salaries.\n- Department Management: Manage and organize different departments within the organization, assigning employees to appropriate departments.\n- Position Management: Define and update job positions and associated salaries, allowing for organizational flexibility and growth.\n- Project Management: Enable the creation and management of projects, including setting start and end dates, and providing detailed project descriptions.\n- Project Assignment: Assign employees to specific projects, facilitating resource allocation and project tracking.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support a growing organization with increasing employee and project numbers.\n- Data Integrity: Ensure accurate and consistent data through foreign key constraints and validation checks.\n- Usability: Provide an intuitive interface for HR personnel to reduce training and operational overhead.\n- Security: Implement access controls to protect sensitive employee and project information.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0235\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `position` (\n  `position_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `position_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `salary` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`position_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `hire_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`position_id`) REFERENCES `position` (`position_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project_assignment` (\n  `assignment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `assigned_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`assignment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_assignment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `project_assignment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
